      "math_academy_id": "e-13695",
      "problem": "What model could represent the division problem below?\n\n$$\n3 \\div \\dfrac{1}{6} = 18\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Consider the following $\\color{red}3$ wholes:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129499/assets/235e19c4e3231eb22e6d43ccadcd90c5694077ec4ce562e6c4f188cfff77545f.png)\n\nTo calculate ${\\color{red}3} \\div \\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}6}$, we need to divide each of $\\color{red}3$ wholes into $\\color{blue}6$ equal parts, as shown below. This gives us the corresponding model for the given division problem.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129499/assets/3b3551ad59a9d5abe2bf03e350f373412959293c68a4f059123fafcbabf72936.png)\n\nWe get ${\\color{red}3} \\times {\\color{blue}6}= 18$ pieces in total.",
